        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T20:17:08Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(slot): a picked Slot stays inside its edges or face\n\nTwo opposite straight edges (or one face / closed ring) picked for a\nSlot now bound the room it may cut in. The pick seeds the slot that\nfills the room into the endpoints and width, in the pick's own\nundoable command (SetOperationGeometry, CreateOperation); generation\nand the preview refuse by name, with the numbers, a slot too wide, too\nlong or placed past the picks (machining2d::SlotBound, world-free, for\nthe Trochoidal slot too); and a picked Slot is judged against the part\n(DepthLaw::Section), so one cut below the picked floor is a Gouge that\nholds the post. With nothing picked the typed endpoints rule as before.\nThe Geometry tab echoes the room or the refusal.\n\nFixes #1504\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
